Fonts
-----

Two kinds, and only one of them is redistributed.

The interface is set in Segoe UI and Consolas, READ FROM WINDOWS at run time.
No Microsoft font file is embedded or shipped.

Behind them, as the fallback for anything those do not cover and for machines
that do not have them, are the faces epaint carries - compiled into
Cutaway.exe through the crate epaint_default_fonts:

    Ubuntu-Light        Ubuntu Font Licence 1.0
    NotoEmoji-Regular   SIL Open Font License 1.1
    Hack-Regular        MIT, with the Bitstream Vera licence for its ancestor
    emoji-icon-font     MIT

Their full licence texts travel inside that crate, under fonts/.

Not bundled
-----------

Windows' own OCR engine reads the text in a picture, and MAPI hands a message
to whichever mail client is installed. Both are components of the operating
system: used, not redistributed.
